    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the timeline, and so do I. The driver marked arrival at 10:17:00 and the GPS trace confirms he was genuinely on scene — the nearest fix (10:17:11) sits 5.75 m from the pickup, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. This was an on-demand trip, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait ran from arrival to 10:22:00, and the driver cancelled at 10:23:30, 390 seconds after arrival. The wait was served. That, however, only opens the door to a fee; it does not satisfy the separate precondition in POL-NS-23.\n\nPOL-NS-23 requires the driver, before cancelling for no-show, to have sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call. The message limb is met — two messages went out (10:17:20 and 10:20:45), both delivered and read. The call limb is not: trip_record.in_app_calls is an empty array, contact_before_cancel.call_count is 0, and the chat log contains only the two text messages and no voice-call entry. No in-app call was placed before the 10:23:30 cancellation. The driver's filing says he 'messaged and called the passenger two times'; the record contradicts the call half of that, the rider's statement ('He never called me') matches the record, and the driver's own advocate did not press the two-call account. (The read receipts do show the messages were read at 10:17:33 and 10:21:22, before the cancellation — that contradicts the rider's suggestion that she saw them only afterwards — but it changes nothing: the message limb was already satisfied, and reading messages cannot supply the missing call.) Because one limb of POL-NS-23 is missing, the fee is voided and the rider is not charged: FULL_REFUND of the 5.00 SGD fee charged, with no driver compensation.\n\nOn the driver's other points: it is accepted that the amount charged is exactly the policy no-show fee of 5.00 SGD, which removes any POL-NS-22 fee-amount referral — but POL-NS-22 transfers the fee to the driver only where the fee stands, and it does not stand. The free-wait and arrival findings (POL-NS-21) are accepted but are not sufficient without POL-NS-23. The rider's advocate proposed NO_ACTION on the basis that the refund is already recorded in the ledger (payment_status REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 5.00); I rule FULL_REFUND because that is the outcome POL-NS-23 itself prescribes where the contact obligation fails, and it matches the 5.00 SGD the fare ledger shows returned to the rider.\n\nNo escalation is needed. Every fact this decision rests on is carried by complete artifacts: the trip record and chat log (both weight_multiplier 1.0) establish the missing call, and the trip record and GPS trace (both 1.0) establish arrival and the wait. The only impaired artifact is the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05062-01 (MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0); under POL-GEN-02(3) it carries no fact, and no no-show clause requires a traffic record, so POL-GEN-26 does not bite. No POL-NS-25 repeat no-show referral arises: the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter. The disputed value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither profile carries a fraud flag, so under POL-NS-26 this AI ruling is final. The 5.00 SGD refund to the rider stands and the driver's request to restore the charge is refused."
